<title>JAPAN: Chiyoda says wins 15 bln yen in orders from GM.</title>
<headline>Chiyoda says wins 15 bln yen in orders from GM.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiyoda Corp said on Tuesday that it had received orders from General Motors Corp to build car manufacturing plants in Thailand and Poland.</p>
<p>The orders are estimated to be worth about 15 billion yen, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The Japanese business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun reported on Tuesday that Chiyoda had also received an order worth 600 million yen from Ford Motor Co to operate part of a Ford car-making plant in Thailand.</p>
<p>However, the company spokesman declined to confirm the report, saying that the deal has not been finalised.</p>
</text>
